  "findings": [
    "T1c: on injected PURE DUST the fitter calls a star significantly flat at least 1007662x more often than significantly steep (169 vs 0 of 167715 injected). The alpha axis is skewed, so the steep tail is NOT a valid mirror for the flat tail and a small steep count certifies nothing. Use the injection-measured type-S rate (T1b) instead.",
    "T3A: against a mark-permutation null the survivor set is a DEFICIT, not an excess: 372 observed against 573 +/- 18 expected (z = -10.9). The flat-slope population avoids clean, high-latitude, low-extinction sky, which is what dust does. The published framing -- 372 survivors, asymmetric at 28.6:1 over the amplitude mirror -- was never compared to this null, and the amplitude mirror does not test sky association at all."
